 78	 * mentioned in prose doesn't get flagged as a code violation. Tracks block-comment state across
 79	 * lines via the mutable `state` object the caller owns. `//` is only treated as a comment start
 80	 * when not immediately preceded by `:` — otherwise `'https://wa.me/...'` string literals (real
 81	 * content in this codebase's Contentful fixtures) would truncate the line early.
 82	 */
 83	function stripComments(line, state) {
 84	  let result = '';
